{"p4": {"friction": "Proposition 4.7 says \"this construction defines a contravariant functor Spec\": the word 'defines' appears inside a proved proposition about an already-introduced symbol, and the defines test does not directly address this. Theorem 1.1 is labelled \"(Corollary 5.2)\" while its hypotheses differ (affine vs FSch^qt), and the rubric has no guidance for restated or intro versions of later results.", "doubt": "Claim 5 (defines vs proves for a functoriality proposition) and claim 6 (whether an intro restatement cross-reference counts as equivalent-to).", "missing_context": "The proofs and the surrounding prose for each result are absent (only statements are given), so I could not check whether the paper says how Theorem 1.1 and Corollary 5.2 relate.", "proposed_change": "Add a near-miss to `defines`: a Proposition or Theorem asserting that an existing construction 'defines a functor' is `proves` (functoriality), not `defines`. Add a rule for intro restatements such as 'Theorem 1.1 (Corollary 5.2)', saying whether they are equivalent-to, generalises or out of scope.", "process_observation": "Claims 2 and 10 are near-duplicates, as are claims 9 and 18; dedup before grading would save effort. Claims 3 and 7 both miss the cited modality of a definition tagged with a bracketed reference."}}
